      "heading": "1. Kharif Season Sowing Status:",
      "text": "-  Kharif  sowing  data  collection  has  started  from  05 th June,  2026  and  the  sowing  is  in  preliminary stage. As on June 05 2026, the area sown under Kharif crops is 72.57 lakh ha (including 54.08 lakh ha in Sugarcane) as compared to 74.61 lakh ha during the corresponding period of last year.",
      "page_number": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Week 1 (05 June  - 11 June 2026):",
      "text": "-  Gradual fall by 2-4°C in maximum temperatures likely  over many parts of Northwest India during 04 th -06 th June and gradual rise by 3-5°C during 07 th -09 th June.\n-  No significant  change  in  maximum  temperatures  likely  over  East  India  till  10 th June  except  Bihar where rise in maximum temperature by 2-3°C till 06 th June.",
      "page_number": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Details of each Segment",
      "text": "-  Maximum temperatures is  likely  to  be  above  normal NW India, East India, NE India, Central India and Gujarat.\n-  Low probability of Heatwave conditions likely over parts of northwest India (Uttar Pradesh) and parts of East India (Bihar, Jharkhand, Odisha, Gangetic West Bengal &amp; Chhattisgarh) and adjoining central India (Madhya Pradesh) on some days of the week.\n-  Above-normal (+1.6 to +3.0°C) to appreciably above-normal (+3.1 to +5.0°C)  maximum temperatures are likely in parts of East  India and the plains of northwest  India, and above-normal maximum temperatures (+1.6 to +3.0°C) are likely over parts of northeast India. Near-normal weekly maximum temperatures (-1.5 to +1.5°C) are likely across the rest of the country during the week .",
      "page_number": 1
    },
